Falsifies `kernel::arch::riscv64::iommu::proofs::the_iommu_is_handed_exactly_the_domain_the_kernel_built`.

The defect is the one this file sets up by example. Every other address this driver hands
the IOMMU (`ddtp`, and both queue bases through `queue_base`) carries its PPN at bits
[53:10], so `(pa >> 12) << 10` appears three times within a screen of `device_context`.
`iosatp` is the odd one out: its PPN sits at [43:0], the way the CPU's `satp` does. Making
`fsc` "match its neighbours" is the edit a tidy reader would make, and the RISC-V page
table entry (PPN at bit 10) makes the same confusion familiar.

The result is worse than a wrong root. `root >> 2` puts address bits 62 and 63 on
`iosatp.MODE`, so for a high enough address the mode stops being Sv39, and MODE 0 is Bare:
translation switched off rather than pointed somewhere wrong.

Unlike the SMMU's falsifications, **this one is probably not invisible to the tests**: on
QEMU's `virt` board every root is wrong under it, so the boot-time confinement test in
`kernel/src/virtio.rs` would most likely fail too. That was reasoned, not run (no riscv64
QEMU boot was taken for this record). The harness is the one that says why.

Expected to fail: `assert!(dc[3] >> 60 == 8, ...)` (MODE, for an unconstrained root) and
`assert!((dc[3] & ((1 << 44) - 1)) << 12 == root, ...)` (the PPN). Confirmed red on
2026-09-25 (UTC), on an aarch64 host through the proof-only module in `arch/mod.rs`.

The sibling harness `no_device_can_reach_another_devices_context` stays green under this
patch: it never builds a context, only locates one.

diff --git a/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs b/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
index 00edbb6c4..1d294b26f 100644
--- a/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@ fn device_context(root: u64, pscid: u16) -> [u64; 8] {
         DC_TC_V,                          // tc: valid, faults reported (DTF clear)
         0,                                // iohgatp: Bare
         (pscid as u64) << TA_PSCID_SHIFT, // ta
-        FSC_MODE_SV39 | (root >> 12),     // fsc = iosatp
+        FSC_MODE_SV39 | ((root >> 12) << 10), // fsc = iosatp
         0,                                // msiptp: MODE Off (notes/riscv-port/iommu.md)
         0,                                // msi_addr_mask
         0,                                // msi_addr_pattern
